WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.944
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.244 --> 00:00:08.328
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.628 --> 00:00:14.137
Unit eleven: Climate Action. In this unit, you will discuss climate change and future targets.

4
00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:16.569
renewable source.

5
00:00:17.269 --> 00:00:22.357
renewable source means a source of energy that is naturally replaced, like wind or sun.

6
00:00:22.657 --> 00:00:25.608
Hydropower is Cambodia's main renewable source.

7
00:00:26.308 --> 00:00:28.914
Your turn. Say: renewable source.

8
00:00:31.614 --> 00:00:33.010
renewable source.

9
00:00:34.017 --> 00:00:35.204
fossil fuel.

10
00:00:35.904 --> 00:00:40.655
fossil fuel means fuel from ancient plants and animals, like coal, oil and gas.

11
00:00:40.955 --> 00:00:43.442
Burning fossil fuels causes air pollution.

12
00:00:44.142 --> 00:00:46.933
Your turn. Say: fossil fuel.

13
00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:50.867
fossil fuel.

14
00:00:51.883 --> 00:00:53.291
sea level rise.

15
00:00:53.991 --> 00:00:56.826
sea level rise means the increase in the height of the ocean.

16
00:00:57.126 --> 00:01:00.136
Sea level rise threatens coastal towns like Kep.

17
00:01:00.836 --> 00:01:03.802
Your turn. Say: sea level rise.

18
00:01:06.502 --> 00:01:08.072
sea level rise.

19
00:01:09.083 --> 00:01:10.270
climate refugee.

20
00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:14.560
climate refugee means a person forced to move because of climate change.

21
00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:18.114
Millions could become climate refugees by 2050.

22
00:01:18.814 --> 00:01:21.768
Your turn. Say: climate refugee.

23
00:01:24.468 --> 00:01:25.817
climate refugee.

24
00:01:26.817 --> 00:01:27.853
solar farm.

25
00:01:28.553 --> 00:01:32.863
solar farm means a large area of solar panels producing electricity.

26
00:01:33.163 --> 00:01:35.743
A new solar farm opened near Kampong Speu.

27
00:01:36.443 --> 00:01:39.165
Your turn. Say: solar farm.

28
00:01:41.865 --> 00:01:42.959
solar farm.

29
00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.230
emissions target.

30
00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:49.357
emissions target means a goal for reducing greenhouse gases.

31
00:01:49.657 --> 00:01:52.284
The country set an ambitious emissions target.

32
00:01:52.984 --> 00:01:55.555
Your turn. Say: emissions target.

33
00:01:58.255 --> 00:01:59.581
emissions target.

34
00:02:00.583 --> 00:02:01.526
net zero.

35
00:02:02.226 --> 00:02:05.178
net zero means removing as much carbon as you produce.

36
00:02:05.478 --> 00:02:08.917
Many companies aim to reach net zero by 2050.

37
00:02:09.617 --> 00:02:11.805
Your turn. Say: net zero.

38
00:02:14.505 --> 00:02:15.576
net zero.

39
00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:17.701
climate summit.

40
00:02:18.401 --> 00:02:22.002
climate summit means an international meeting about climate change.

41
00:02:22.302 --> 00:02:24.522
World leaders met at the climate summit.

42
00:02:25.222 --> 00:02:27.596
Your turn. Say: climate summit.

43
00:02:30.296 --> 00:02:31.483
climate summit.

44
00:02:32.483 --> 00:02:34.483
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:34.783 --> 00:02:37.166
Where do you think we'll be in 2050?

46
00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:41.181
I hope most countries will have reached net zero.

47
00:02:42.483 --> 00:02:44.692
Will we still be burning fossil fuels?

48
00:02:45.983 --> 00:02:49.678
Some, but by then we'll have built many more solar farms.

49
00:02:50.983 --> 00:02:52.623
What about sea level rise?

50
00:02:53.917 --> 00:02:59.213
Coastal cities will be adapting, and leaders will still be meeting at climate summits.

51
00:03:00.517 --> 00:03:04.060
Grammar focus: Future continuous and future perfect.

52
00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:07.823
Use the future continuous for actions in progress at a future time.

53
00:03:08.123 --> 00:03:11.817
Use the future perfect for actions completed before a future time.

54
00:03:12.117 --> 00:03:18.494
For example: In 2050, we will be using renewable energy, and we will have reached net zero.

55
00:03:18.794 --> 00:03:24.270
Compare: at 8 p.m. I'll be eating (in progress) vs by 8 p.m. I'll have eaten (finished).

56
00:03:25.283 --> 00:03:28.005
Now read and listen. Racing to Net Zero.

57
00:03:28.305 --> 00:03:34.032
At recent climate summits, many countries promised to reach net zero by 2050.

58
00:03:35.317 --> 00:03:38.814
To succeed, the world will have to stop relying on fossil fuels.

59
00:03:40.117 --> 00:03:44.624
By 2030, many nations will have doubled their solar farms and wind power.

60
00:03:45.917 --> 00:03:49.727
Meanwhile, coastal communities will be preparing for sea level rise.

61
00:03:51.017 --> 00:03:54.885
If targets are missed, millions of people may become climate refugees.

62
00:03:56.183 --> 00:03:58.545
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:58.845 --> 00:04:01.414
Removing as much carbon as you produce is blank.

64
00:04:01.714 --> 00:04:06.110
A, net zero. B, fossil fuel. C, sea level rise.

65
00:04:10.117 --> 00:04:12.139
The answer is A: net zero.

66
00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:17.287
By 2040, scientists blank a cure for many diseases.

67
00:04:17.587 --> 00:04:21.147
A, will be finding. B, will have found. C, find.

68
00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:27.300
The answer is B: will have found.

69
00:04:28.817 --> 00:04:31.594
At this time tomorrow, I blank to Siem Reap.

70
00:04:31.894 --> 00:04:35.362
A, will be driving. B, will have driven. C, drive.

71
00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:41.303
The answer is A: will be driving.

72
00:04:42.817 --> 00:04:44.689
Coal, oil and gas are blank.

73
00:04:44.989 --> 00:04:49.617
A, renewable sources. B, fossil fuels. C, solar farms.

74
00:04:53.617 --> 00:04:55.732
The answer is B: fossil fuels.

75
00:04:57.217 --> 00:05:00.354
According to the text, what may happen if targets are missed?

76
00:05:00.654 --> 00:05:06.653
A, more solar farms. B, people may become climate refugees. C, sea levels will fall.

77
00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:14.403
The answer is B: people may become climate refugees.

78
00:05:15.917 --> 00:05:21.077
Now it's your turn to speak. What will your country have done to fight climate change by 2040?

79
00:05:26.377 --> 00:05:32.440
By 2040, Cambodia will have built many solar farms, and people will be using more electric vehicles.

80
00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:34.356
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:40.069
Great work today! You learned eight new words and future continuous and future perfect.

82
00:05:40.369 --> 00:05:44.658
Today's value is caring for nature. Care for plants, birds and our planet.

83
00:05:44.958 --> 00:05:47.274
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

84
00:05:47.574 --> 00:05:50.133
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

